    "evidence": "Independently reviewed every assigned changed/new member in the authoritative narration and full-kit context, retaining the exact-source/SHA cached passes for unchanged members without replaying them. Both outstanding repairs are resolved: exact repository revision comparison establishes preservation of the separate six-packet baseline, and complete reviewed plan hash/version binding prevents changes to owners, TTLs, timestamps, endpoints, metadata or event order from passing unnoticed. Explicit selected RR owner/type checks now support the verifier's stated semantics. Supplied current Linux receipts show shipped and rebuilt PASS and fail-closed corrupt-capture and mutated-plan tests; no new local execution is claimed by this review. Full exercise scope remains enabled through the client-facing alias/multiple-address/IPv6/history fixture, upstream-attribution fixture, no-DNS fixture and separate supplemental exercise. Historical receipts are explicitly historical. GUI and Windows steps remain unexecuted student instructions; no historical incident finding, application hostname proof, cache explanation or completed learner homework is inferred."
